      "synthesis": {
        "main_text_has_explicit_synthesis": true,
        "si_used": false,
        "procedure": "A mixture of 2-hydroxy-5-methylisophthalaldehyde (33 mg, 0.2 mmol) and 2-aminoethanol (15 mg, 0.25 mmol) in MeCN/MeOH (8/8 mL) was stirred and heated at 80 °C for 1 h (solution turned dark yellow). LnCl3·6H2O (Ln = Gd; 37 mg, 0.1 mmol), Mn(OAc)2·4H2O (49 mg, 0.2 mmol), and triethylamine (30 mg, 0.3 mmol) were then added in order. The brown solution was stirred under ambient conditions for 2 h, filtered, and small black crystals of 1-Ln formed as the solution nearly dried.",
